Unifi has become stricter in what keys provided in requests.

```json
{
    "meta": {"rc": "error", "msg": "api.err.InvalidPayload"},
    "data": [
        {
            "validationError": {"field": "portconf_id", "pattern": "[\\d\\w]+"},
            "rc": "error",
            "msg": "api.err.InvalidValue",
        }
    ],
}
```

Rename `revert_transaction` to `reject_transaction`; 
Checks if the caller of `reject_transaction` is the sender, receiver or mediator across any of the legs;
Emit event instead of storing the sender's proof;

Closes #148 

## Example

```rust
let mut group = StreamGroup::new();
group.insert(stream::once(2));
group.insert(stream::once(4));

let mut out = 0;
while let Some(num) = group.next().await {
    out += num;
}
assert_eq!(out, 6);
```

